# React Web Rules

Use `src/features/` for feature code. Route definitions stay thin; feature screens, logic, API calls, components, hooks, and types live under the relevant feature.

- Keep a component in its parent file when it is small and parent-specific.
- Extract a component only when it has meaningful independent behavior, real reuse, or makes an otherwise unclear parent understandable.
- Extract a hook only for real reuse or when it creates a clearer boundary in an overloaded parent.
- Use local state by default. Use global state only for genuinely application-wide state.
- Use Zustand as the default global client store when the project's approved stack includes it. Keep temporary global UI state separate from durable persisted state such as a session.
- Read Zustand through narrow selectors; do not consume a whole combined store from ordinary components.
- Use TanStack Query for server state. Do not duplicate server state in local or global state without a specific UI reason.
- Keep query keys, query or mutation options, invalidation, and feature-level success/error feedback in the feature `api/` location. Configure `QueryClient` once at the app root.
- Use Formik and Yup for forms. Do not mirror form fields in local `useState`.
- Use `useEffect` only for real side effects. Do not add `useMemo` or `useCallback` without a demonstrated need.
- Mount error, query, theme, and global UI providers only at the application root. Do not duplicate them inside features.
- Keep tokenized colors, spacing, typography, and layout values in the approved theme source.
- Keep one shared HTTP client. When the approved auth architecture has refresh tokens, keep token refresh and session reset in that API boundary rather than feature requests.

## Styling

Use `styled-components` only.

- Every rendered component root is a styled wrapper named `Container`.
- Every rendered `Container` has a meaningful, unique kebab-case `id`.
- Style internal elements through short, role-based classes nested inside `Container`, such as `header`, `content`, `actions`, `list`, or `item`.
- Keep styles close to the component. Do not create a separate styles file merely to move a small `Container` declaration.
- Do not introduce CSS Modules, Tailwind, inline style objects, or another styling system without approval.
